:: TruthToThief
<h2 class="story-title">Truth Honors Truth</h2>

"You should be ashamed," the sethani said with dignity, "casting such aspersions on a father's concern for his daughter!"

Then she narrated the whole story in detail—how she went with desire, how the thakur called her daughter, how everything changed in a single moment.

Khapariyau the Thief believed her. The truth rang clear in her voice.

He made her his dharma sister and quietly went his way, disappointed. But he was, after all, a subject in this thikana. He couldn't risk looting the thakur's adopted daughter.

All his hard labor digging the tunnel was worth nothing but the labor itself.

